# Bloodline Component Rules

## Core Philosophy

Build systems, not isolated pages.

Components should be:
- reusable
- composable
- scalable
- predictable
- typed
- section-driven

Avoid:
- one-off component chaos
- duplicated layout structures
- tightly coupled UI

---

## Component Taxonomy

Use the official component structure:

```txt
components/
  ui/
  layout/
  sections/
  cta/
  seo/
  motion/
  gallery/
  shared/
```

Do not invent random component folders unnecessarily.

---

## UI Component Rules

`ui/` contains:
- primitives
- reusable low-level UI
- reusable variants

Examples:

```txt
Button
Card
Badge
Input
Dialog
Accordion
```

UI primitives should remain:
- generic
- reusable
- token-driven

Avoid:
- business-specific logic inside UI primitives

---

## Section Component Rules

`sections/` contains:
- reusable business sections
- page composition blocks

Examples:

```txt
HeroSection
ReviewPreviewSection
StudioStandardsSection
FAQSection
```

Sections should:
- receive structured props
- remain reusable
- support multiple page contexts

Avoid:
- hardcoded region copy
- inline fetch logic
- duplicated section variants

---

## Layout Component Rules

`layout/` contains:
- structural wrappers
- navigation
- footer
- containers
- grids

Layout components should:
- remain structural
- avoid business-specific behavior

---

## CTA Component Rules

`cta/` contains:
- CTA systems
- WhatsApp interactions
- conversion modals
- sticky CTA bars

CTA behavior should remain:
- centralized
- reusable
- config-driven

Avoid:
- scattered CTA implementations

---

## Motion Component Rules

`motion/` contains:
- reusable animation wrappers
- reveal systems
- hover systems
- stagger systems

Motion components should:
- remain lightweight
- remain reusable
- follow motion guidelines

Avoid:
- section-specific animation duplication

---

## SEO Component Rules

`seo/` contains:
- schema helpers
- breadcrumb rendering
- metadata support components

Avoid:
- duplicating SEO rendering logic across routes

---

## Shared Component Rules

`shared/` contains:
- small reusable business fragments
- repeated micro-patterns

Examples:

```txt
SectionHeading
ProofStrip
TrustBadge
```

Avoid:
- oversized shared abstractions

---

## Prop Rules

Components should receive:
- typed props
- structured data
- prepared content

Avoid:
- hidden assumptions
- untyped object props
- business logic embedded in UI

Preferred:

```ts
interface HeroSectionProps {
  heading: string;
  subheading: string;
}
```

---

## Data Fetching Rules

Components should NOT:
- fetch Airtable directly
- normalize external data
- perform business orchestration

Data preparation belongs in:
- route loaders
- utilities
- server functions
- lib helpers

Components should focus on:
```txt
presentation
```

---

## Region Rules

Components must remain:
- region-agnostic
- reusable

All regional content should flow through:
- props
- config
- helpers

Avoid:
- hardcoded regional copy

Forbidden:

```tsx
<h1>Bangkok Tattoo Studio</h1>
```

---

## Variant Rules

Use reusable variant systems.

Examples:
- button variants
- card variants
- spacing variants
- heading variants

Preferred:
- CVA
- centralized variant logic

Avoid:
- duplicated styling branches

---

## Composition Rules

Pages should be assembled from:
- reusable sections
- reusable wrappers
- reusable patterns

Avoid:
- giant monolithic page files
- duplicated page anatomy

---

## Section Rhythm Rules

Pages should follow:

```txt
Attention
→ Trust
→ Proof
→ Depth
→ Conversion
```

Avoid:
- filler sections
- decorative clutter
- inconsistent sequencing

---

## Reusability Rules

Before creating a new component:
- check existing variants
- check reusable systems
- check section compatibility

Avoid:
- near-duplicate components
- copy-paste section architecture

---

## Typography Rules

Components must follow:
- uppercase heading rules
- token-based styling
- approved typography system

Avoid:
- arbitrary font usage
- inconsistent heading hierarchy

---

## Styling Rules

Use:
- semantic tokens
- reusable spacing systems
- centralized variants

Avoid:
- random arbitrary styling
- duplicated utility combinations
- hardcoded color values

---

## Accessibility Rules

All components should support:
- semantic HTML
- keyboard navigation
- aria support where necessary
- readable contrast
- reduced motion support

Accessibility is mandatory.

---

## Performance Rules

Components should:
- minimize hydration
- avoid unnecessary client rendering
- lazy load heavy media where appropriate

Avoid:
- oversized interactive wrappers
- client-side rendering creep

---

## Naming Rules

Use PascalCase.

Examples:

```txt
HeroSection.tsx
ReviewCard.tsx
TattooStyleGrid.tsx
```

Avoid:
- vague component names
- inconsistent naming patterns

---

## File Size Rules

Avoid:
- giant 1000-line components
- monolithic section logic

Prefer:
- decomposition
- reusable fragments
- clean separation

---

## AI Safety Rules

AI-generated components must:
- follow existing patterns
- reuse systems
- preserve architecture consistency
- avoid unnecessary invention

Do not generate:
- disconnected UI systems
- one-off layout architectures
- duplicated section patterns

---

## Forbidden Patterns

Never introduce:

- hardcoded regional copy
- duplicated sections
- duplicated layout systems
- direct Airtable calls in components
- oversized monolithic pages
- random component folders
- business logic inside primitives
- client-rendered SEO sections

---

## Final Principle

Every component decision should reinforce:

- scalability
- composability
- consistency
- performance
- SEO safety
- premium presentation
- architectural clarity

If a component weakens those goals, do not implement it.